and let them fire me.

00:06:26.345 --> 00:06:27.221
Cool, huh?

00:06:27.221 --> 00:06:29.306
H-How exactly?

00:06:29.306 --> 00:06:34.520
That's when my childhood friend Nina here
introduced me to Rat Productions.

00:06:35.521 --> 00:06:41.151
But, even after changing agencies,
I'm still not getting any work.

00:06:41.151 --> 00:06:43.612
I'm completely forgotten, anyway...

00:06:43.612 --> 00:06:46.073
Th-That's not true, Roko-<i>sempai</i>!

00:06:46.073 --> 00:06:50.577
I'm happy I get to work with someone
I respect like you, Roko-<i>sempai</i>!

00:06:50.577 --> 00:06:51.787
Ino...

00:06:51.787 --> 00:06:57.376
I may be older than you, but please take care
of me from here on out, Roko-<i>sempai</i>!

00:06:57.751 --> 00:06:59.002
"1st year in high school" "155cm"
"2nd year in high school"
"Self-Proclaimed 140cm"

00:07:00.838 --> 00:07:04.633
And what do you think you're doing, Hoho?
Is that supposed to be a secret camera?

00:07:04.633 --> 00:07:08.971
Ah, this is for the new program,
so don't mind me.

00:07:08.971 --> 00:07:10.722
A new program?

00:07:10.722 --> 00:07:12.975
Yup, that's right!

00:07:12.975 --> 00:07:17.688
It'll determine whether they'll
demolish Mouse House... or not.

00:07:17.688 --> 00:07:18.772
Huh?

00:07:18.772 --> 00:07:22.317
What?! Demolishing Mouse House?!

00:07:22.317 --> 00:07:23.402
That's right.

00:07:23.402 --> 00:07:25.696
Housing an unpopular former child actor...

00:07:25.696 --> 00:07:27.573
...an unpopular model...

00:07:27.573 --> 00:07:30.033
...and an unpopular musician...

00:07:30.033 --> 00:07:34.121
...seems to be becoming
a burden for the agency...

00:07:34.121 --> 00:07:37.541
Th-Then, why take in an aspiring idol?

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:40.419
That's because...

00:07:40.419 --> 00:07:44.339
...I've got a grand recovery plan right here!

00:07:44.339 --> 00:07:45.257
Huh?

00:07:45.257 --> 00:07:45.799
"Proposal"
"New Idol TV Program"
"Dropout Idol Fruit Tart" "Approved"
Huh?

00:07:45.799 --> 00:07:47.176
"Proposal"
"New Idol TV Program"
"Dropout Idol Fruit Tart" "Approved"
Dropout idol?

00:07:47.176 --> 00:07:49.261
"Proposal"
"New Idol TV Program"
"Dropout Idol Fruit Tart" "Approved"
What's this new idol TV program about?

00:07:49.261 --> 00:07:51.972
In order to save Mouse House from demolition,

00:07:51.972 --> 00:07:54.933
we'll have you girls form an idol group,

00:07:54.933 --> 00:08:00.731
and make some money by producing a five-minute
weekly variety show for a whole year!

00:08:00.731 --> 00:08:02.065
What?!

00:08:02.065 --> 00:08:03.901
The group name is

00:08:03.901 --> 00:08:05.444
Fruit Tart!

00:08:05.444 --> 00:08:07.529
Fruit Tart?!

00:09:47.754 --> 00:09:48.922
"We're off to Higako!"

00:09:48.922 --> 00:09:51.466
"We're off to Higako!"
We're off to Higako!

00:09:51.466 --> 00:09:53.010
"We're off to Higako!"

00:09:55.846 --> 00:09:58.348
My first morning in Tokyo.

00:09:58.348 --> 00:10:01.810
An unfamiliar ceiling, a new smell...

00:10:03.103 --> 00:10:09.985
That's right! Starting today,
I'm an idol along with my wonderful seniors!

00:10:09.985 --> 00:10:12.279
Good morning, everyone!

00:10:13.864 --> 00:10:15.991
I really don't want to do this idol thing.

00:10:15.991 --> 00:10:16.909
What?

00:10:18.368 --> 00:10:21.538
I'm really an actor, you know?

00:10:21.538 --> 00:10:24.249
I'm not confident with
my singing or dancing, either.

00:10:24.249 --> 00:10:28.295
What? Really? I'm actually
looking forward to it.

00:10:28.295 --> 00:10:32.257
In any case, it's hard to believe
the agency's strapped for cash.

00:10:32.257 --> 00:10:34.218
We've been eating all three meals every day.

00:10:34.218 --> 00:10:36.303
What do you think, Inocchi?

00:10:36.303 --> 00:10:38.889
Wh-What's that you're eating for breakfast?

00:10:38.889 --> 00:10:41.433
Oh. A large serving of
the morning curry, of course.

00:10:41.433 --> 00:10:42.601
Um...

00:10:42.601 --> 00:10:46.563
It seems like everyone's able
to eat curry for breakfast here...

00:10:46.563 --> 00:10:48.232
Do you think less of us now?

00:10:48.232 --> 00:10:50.359
Our curry is amazing, you know?!

00:10:50.359 --> 00:10:53.654
It's a special dish that's gone through
extensive research and development!

00:10:53.654 --> 00:10:56.365
Everything tastes delicious in curry.

00:10:56.365 --> 00:10:59.701
It's cheap and nutritious! And once you
make a batch, it'll last for months!

00:10:59.701 --> 00:11:01.119
Yup, yup!

00:11:01.119 --> 00:11:02.913
What?! For months?!

00:11:02.913 --> 00:11:07.292
It's a dish that can be eaten for all three
meals every day and fuels us common folks!

00:11:07.292 --> 00:11:09.586
Um... What do you mean by every day?

00:11:09.586 --> 00:11:12.256
Don't tell me this is all you eat...

00:11:13.924 --> 00:11:15.092
Anyway,

00:11:15.092 --> 00:11:18.178
are you okay with forming
an idol group with us, Ino?

00:11:18.178 --> 00:11:24.101
I'd much rather form a group with you all
than go solo. It feels a lot more reassuring.

00:11:24.101 --> 00:11:26.520
Oh, okay...

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:31.692
So just letting you know,
yesterday's idol group plan is totally official.

00:11:31.692 --> 00:11:33.944
I never said I'd be an idol.

00:11:33.944 --> 00:11:35.028
What choice do you have?

00:11:35.028 --> 00:11:39.658
Do you think you can make more money than
it's worth to sell this dormitory yourselves?

00:11:40.617 --> 00:11:43.579
Y-Yeah, well, we could pick up part-time jobs.

00:11:43.579 --> 00:11:45.122
A part-time job, huh?

00:11:45.122 --> 00:11:47.749
Sure, that's not a bad idea...

00:11:47.749 --> 00:11:50.169
"Mouse House Management/Operation Estimate"
"100,000,000 yen"
Do you really think you can pay this amount?

00:11:51.044 --> 00:11:53.255
If we live off just curry for 30 years...

00:11:53.255 --> 00:11:55.257
Don't convert it into curry...

00:11:55.257 --> 00:12:00.012
But think about it! You'll all be in trouble
without Mouse House, right?

00:12:00.012 --> 00:12:02.598
Ino, you're from Okayama.

00:12:02.598 --> 00:12:04.016
Roko's from Toyama.

00:12:04.016 --> 00:12:05.684
Nina's from Ishikawa.

00:12:05.684 --> 00:12:08.854
Hayu, you pretty much ran away
from home to live at Mouse House.

00:12:08.854 --> 00:12:09.855
Boo.

00:12:09.855 --> 00:12:11.523
And most importantly...

00:12:11.523 --> 00:12:14.276
"Roaring..."
...I won't have a place to live!

00:12:14.276 --> 00:12:16.069
"Roaring..."
So this is really only about yourself!

00:12:17.196 --> 00:12:21.950
That was just a joke, but I worked hard
to get this job, you know?

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:24.953
Roko and Nina, why are you both
so reluctant to become idols?

00:12:24.953 --> 00:12:25.871
What?!

00:12:25.871 --> 00:12:32.336
Th-That's because...
I'm shy when it comes to bikini modeling.

00:12:32.336 --> 00:12:37.132
I would have to do those things
if I become an idol, right?

00:12:37.132 --> 00:12:41.345
What? You're not trying to
pick a fight with all of us, are you?

00:12:41.345 --> 00:12:43.430
N-No! Of course not!

00:12:44.431 --> 00:12:46.141
And what exactly are you doing, Roko?

00:12:46.141 --> 00:12:48.977
I-I absolutely refuse to become an idol!

00:12:48.977 --> 00:12:53.065
I'll never sell myself as everyone's clown!
I'm never getting out of here!

00:12:53.065 --> 00:12:54.775
Never...?

00:12:54.775 --> 00:12:57.027
You're acting like a spoiled child right now.

00:12:57.027 --> 00:12:59.112
Wow! It's bagworm Roko!

00:12:59.112 --> 00:13:00.405
So cute...

00:13:00.405 --> 00:13:05.118
Well, actually... I think there's a healthy
demand for idols to act like that.

00:13:05.118 --> 00:13:07.412
Urgh! D-Don't tease me!

00:13:07.412 --> 00:13:10.666
I-It's okay, you can
come out, Roko. Tch, tch, tch...

00:13:10.666 --> 00:13:13.126
Agh! I'm not a fox, you know?!

00:13:13.126 --> 00:13:14.670
Ah, I forgot to mention this.

00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:19.633
Idols get to promote
all sorts of sweets, remember?

00:13:19.633 --> 00:13:21.134
What? That's all it took?!

00:13:21.134 --> 00:13:25.097
N-No! I won't be tempted by sweets!

00:13:25.097 --> 00:13:28.684
Well, I invite you both
to think about it carefully.

00:13:28.684 --> 00:13:33.647
Think about all those idols
who went on to become great actors.

00:13:33.647 --> 00:13:37.651
Do idols really sell themselves
with sexiness nowadays?

00:13:37.651 --> 00:13:42.197
And most importantly, think about
how many CDs idols sell nowadays.

00:13:42.197 --> 00:13:45.450
A-A million servings of curry-worth!

00:13:48.495 --> 00:13:51.498
I feel like I'm getting forced into
doing this, after all...

00:13:52.374 --> 00:13:55.794
But, we're all in this together,
so let's do our best!

00:13:55.794 --> 00:13:57.379
That's right, Roko!

00:13:57.379 --> 00:13:59.423
I'll try to do my best, too.

00:13:59.423 --> 00:14:03.802
All righty then. Why don't we
dive right in to shooting episode one?

00:14:03.802 --> 00:14:05.012
Already?

00:14:05.012 --> 00:14:07.472
Don't we have a film crew or something?

00:14:07.472 --> 00:14:11.101
You said it was a variety show,
but what are the specific details?

00:14:11.101 --> 00:14:14.897
You girls are funny. I'm the
sole member of the film crew!

00:14:14.897 --> 00:14:19.693
The show is a documentary on the everyday
efforts of an idol group formed from dropouts.

00:14:21.028 --> 00:14:25.782
And let's be real, think about how we,
at Mouse House, got this big job...

00:14:25.782 --> 00:14:27.201
We're cheap...

00:14:27.201 --> 00:14:28.118
Ah...

